        "title": "fix(ui): hide empty native session categories",
        "body": "Related: #104717\n\n## What Problem This Solves\n\nFixes an issue where users with no Codex or Claude Code sessions would see empty native-session categories and a `0` count in the Control UI sidebar.\n\n## Why This Change Was Made\n\nSuppress exhausted empty catalogs at the shared sidebar render boundary. An empty page with a continuation cursor stays visible and loadable, so pagination and later-discovered sessions remain reachable.\n\n## User Impact\n\nEmpty Codex and Claude Code categories no longer occupy sidebar space. Populated and paginated native-session categories continue to work as before.\n\n## Evidence\n\n- Before: the regression test failed against the prior implementation because the empty Codex section rendered with count `0`.\n- After: Blacksmith Testbox `tbx_01kxd30tzbkmvv4pxx48fweh0b` passed 40 sidebar component tests and 2 Chromium native-session E2E tests.\n- Changed-surface validation: `pnpm check:changed` passed its formatting, core-test typecheck, UI typecheck, lint, and guard lanes on the same Testbox.\n- Fresh autoreview accepted and prompted the pagination edge-case fix; the final review reported no accepted or actionable findings.\n\nAI-assisted: yes.\n",
